// XFAIL: DF-235b the OTHER half of the same gap (see
// const_expression_range_unchecked_narrow.saw): a constant EXPRESSION
// reaching a repeat literal's value never adopts the declared element
// width, so out-of-range is not merely unchecked — the value (and its
// backing storage) is silently carried at PLATFORM width instead of the
// declared narrower one. `1 << 20` does not fit `UInt16`, but
// `[1 << 20; 2]` at `[UInt16; 2]` compiles clean and prints the
// UNTRUNCATED `1048576`, meaning the actual element width disagrees with
// what the declared Saw type claims.
//
// SAME SYMPTOM, confirmed by direct compile (not re-pinned, per obligation
// 4 — see DF-235b's tracker entry for the full matrix): an Optional payload
// slot (`let o: UInt16? = 1 << 20`), the `??` operand
// (`absent ?? (1 << 20)`), and a UNIFORM plain array literal whose elements
// are all const expressions (`[1 << 3, 1 << 4]` at `[UInt16; 2]` — no
// `insert_value` crash since every element agrees on the same wrong width,
// unlike the MIXED case in array_literal_const_element_ice.saw, DF-235a).
//
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: does not fit in `UInt16`

func main() {
    let r: [UInt16; 2] = [1 << 20; 2]
    print("{r[0]}")
}
